WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.159
Speaker 1: I don't want to spend a ton of
time on this, but it is important just to

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:04.710
follow up with some of these things.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:12.570
You might remember that when Cassidy Hutchinson
of the WHO worked with Mark Meadows, Trump's

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:17.060
former chief of staff, when Cassidy Hutchinson
testified before the January six committee

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.060
and made a number of different explosive claims
about Donald Trump and Secret Service and

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.680
all of these different things.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:28.160
There were anecdotally messages, statements
from Secret Service saying that's not true

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.029
and we're willing to testify under oath.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:33.560
And the January six committee said, great,
come in and testify under oath.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.800
And then they didn't.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.380
Why haven't they done it?

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:40.310
Well, we have to sort of speculate a little
bit, but here is Adam Kinzinger, one of the

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:44.850
few Republicans on the January six committee
saying we haven't been able to talk to them.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:49.250
I mean, listen, they said they said we'll
talk to you and they just don't come in.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.870
Speaker 2: So we want answers to that.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:57.520
We heard through anonymous sources in the
media that the Secret Service agents present

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:04.190
when Cassidy Hutchison talked about the heated
argument in the limo, the president's beasts,

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.930
that they were eager to talk to us.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.530
We haven't been able to talk to them yet either.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.830
We have our doors wide open.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:15.170
They just have to do it under oath so that
on top of again, we just have a lot of people

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.360
coming forward with pieces of the puzzle,
maybe pieces of information, maybe Cassidy

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.180
Hutchison or Sarah MATTHEWS inspired them.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.110
And so we're going to work on beginning to
write our report, but keep this investigation

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.950
wide open and getting more and more information.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.610
Speaker 1: So, listen, they all came forward.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.830
A bunch of them came forward and they said,
we're willing to testify.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.900
Secret Service agent reportedly willing to
testify.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.740
Trump did not lunged at him.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.750
This is from The Guardian.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.850
And this was right after the testimony of
Cassidy Hutchinson and then a bunch of different

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.580
other media outlets reported on this.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.810
CNN and other outlets reported the pushback
on the alleged Secret Service incident from

00:01:54.810 --> 00:02:00.100
Tony or Nadeau, also a deputy chief of staff
in the Trump White House, Robert Engle, Trump's

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.500
security chief, and on and on and on.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.890
And the committee members said, we welcome
you to be here under oath, of course.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.890
And really, Cassidy Hutchinson was under oath.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:17.780
What is the value of Secret Service agents
showing up not under oath and refuting the

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.780
claims?

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.780
Let's get everybody under oath.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.000
So then we can actually say we have conflicting
under oath statements.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.530
We continue to have only one set of claims
made under oath.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.590
And of course, it wasn't surprising to me.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.450
I've been tweeting about it for weeks.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.650
They haven't testified.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.940
Why haven't they testified?

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:36.970
We don't know.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.530
They're law enforcement.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:43.360
One would think they don't have an issue in
principle with being under oath.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.130
But if you won't testify under oath about
the things you saw while working for the Secret

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.210
Service.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.520
To me, that's a red flag.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.440
And of course, in courts of law, we don't
consider people's silence as indicative of

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.440
guilt.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.239
But when you come out and you say, we'll testify,
we'll talk about it, we didn't see what Cassidy

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:01.250
Hutchinson said and then you're welcomed.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:05.340
Great show up, take an oath, just like she
did, and tell us what you saw.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.599
And then they're missing.

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:11.440
It is completely reasonable in the court of
public opinion to say maybe they weren't telling

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.980
the truth and maybe Cassidy Hutchinson is.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:17.630
One other note on the Cassidy Hutchinson testimony.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:25.220
Pat Cipollone, the former White House counsel
in his under oath testimony, he didn't dispute

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:30.560
the things that Cassidy Hutchinson said with
some he claimed privilege, attorney client

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.390
privilege with Donald Trump.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:37.310
With some he did a sort of I don't recall
or I can't necessarily speak to that.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:42.660
But he went under oath and didn't refute any
of the things that Cassidy Hutchinson said.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.840
So still waiting for the Secret Service agents
to come in.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.010
Not surprising that they haven't, and I don't
expect them to follow me on Twitter at David

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.010
Pakman.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.080
Let me know what you make of the latest absence
of secret.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.070
Service agents who were just weeks ago so
ready to testify.

